# API Information


main: {
  kit: {
    info: {
      contact: {
        url: "https://abdoastore.store/"
      }
      description: "Abdo Store API offers a range of social media marketing services, providing users with access to tools for enhancing their online presence. It supports services like account management, balance loading, and order placement, all aimed at improving social media engagement. The API is designed for ease of use with robust customer support available 24/7."
      servers: [
        {
          description: "Production server"
          url: "https://abdoastore.store"
        }
      ]
      title: "Abdo Store API"
      version: "1.0.0"
      tagline: "Social media marketing tools for account management, balance top-ups, and order placement"
      homepage: "https://abdoastore.store"
      docs_url: "https://freepublicapis.com/abdo-store-api"
      license_short: "No licence specified by the provider."
      license_md: `- No explicit licence is published by the API provider.
- Treat all data and endpoints as the property of Abdo Store; consult the provider before redistributing responses.
- The community catalogue page on freepublicapis.com currently lists this API as non-functional, so availability is not guaranteed.`
      about_md: `Abdo Store API exposes a small set of operations for a social media marketing (SMM) panel run at [abdoastore.store](https://abdoastore.store). It is aimed at resellers and end users who want to manage an account, top up a balance, and place orders against the panel's catalogue of services.

What you typically interact with:

- Account operations — sign-in / profile state for the panel user.
- Balance operations — loading or checking the funds used to pay for orders.
- Service catalogue — the list of social media engagement services the panel offers.
- Order operations — submitting and tracking orders against those services.

The provider advertises 24/7 customer support. No authentication scheme, rate limits, or endpoint contracts are published in a machine-readable form, and the freepublicapis.com catalogue currently reports the upstream as unreachable, so callers should be prepared for downtime and verify behaviour against the live panel before integrating.`
      entity_desc: {
        account: "Represents the panel user's account — profile, credentials, and session state used to authorise other calls."
        order: "Represents an order placed against the panel for a given social media service, including its status and lifecycle."
        service: "Represents an item in the SMM service catalogue (the social media engagement products the panel sells) that orders are placed against."
      }
      auth: false
    }
  }
}
